Each actual bug or finding should be displayed in a structured card containing applicable fields such as:
- Bug title.
- Description.
- Severity, if available.
- Affected file or location, if known.
- Evidence or source.
- Status.
- Suggested next step.

Use distinct but accessible severity treatments.

Do not fabricate bugs or security vulnerabilities to fill empty space.

#### Empty state

If no bugs are available, show a friendly ghost sitting beside an empty gravestone.

Text:

`No bugs in this graveyard. Yet.`

Supporting copy:

`Summon a repository and investigate its codebase to uncover what needs attention.`

CTA:

`INVESTIGATE A REPOSITORY`

#### Interaction design

Provide filters or sorting only when supported by the underlying data.

Use small pumpkin or lantern details as decorative accents. Keep all bug information readable.

