### 15. RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Design the entire product for desktop, tablet, and mobile.

#### Desktop

- A compact top navigation or sidebar.
- A spacious main content area.
- Multi-column dashboard grids.
- A prominent repository-summoning panel.
- Balanced decorative illustrations.
- Clear visual separation between primary and secondary modules.

#### Tablet

- Collapse multi-column grids as needed.
- Maintain comfortable text sizes.
- Reduce decorative elements that compete with content.
- Keep repository inputs and main actions prominent.

#### Mobile

- Single-column content.
- Compact navigation.
- Full-width inputs and primary buttons.
- Readable code blocks with controlled horizontal overflow.
- Stacked analysis cards.
- Appropriately sized ghost and pumpkin illustrations.
- No horizontal page overflow.
- Touch targets of approximately 44 × 44 CSS pixels where practical.

Do not simply shrink the desktop interface. Recompose the layout for smaller screens.

Decorations should adapt to screen size. Reduce the number of floating elements on mobile if they affect performance or readability.

