### 18. ACCESSIBILITY & USABILITY

The theme must never compromise usability.

Ensure:
- Strong text contrast.
- Keyboard-accessible navigation.
- Visible focus indicators.
- Accessible form labels.
- Meaningful button names.
- Screen-reader-friendly status messages.
- Error messages that explain how to recover.
- No critical information communicated through color alone.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Reasonable text sizes.
- Appropriate touch-target sizes.
- Decorative illustrations hidden from assistive technology when they provide no information.

Keep pumpkins, ghosts, and lanterns away from important text and controls.

Avoid using the same icon to represent several unrelated actions.

